Student Management System

Overview

The Student Management System is a console-based Java application developed to manage student records efficiently. It allows users to perform essential student management operations through a simple menu-driven interface. The project is built using Java, JDBC, and MySQL, providing hands-on experience with database connectivity and CRUD operations.

Features

- Add a new student
- View all student records
- Search for a student by ID
- Update student details
- Delete student records
- Input validation for user entries
- Menu-driven console interface

Technologies Used

- Java
- JDBC (Java Database Connectivity)
- MySQL
- Eclipse IDE
- Git & GitHub

Project Structure

- "Main.java" – Application entry point
- "Student.java" – Student model class
- "StudentDAO.java" – Database operations (CRUD)
- "DBConnection.java" – MySQL database connection
- Other supporting classes as required

Database

This project uses MySQL to store student information.

Example fields:
Student ID
Name
Department
Age
Email

How to Run

-Clone this repository.
-Open the project in Eclipse or your preferred Java IDE.
-Create the required MySQL database and table.
-Update the database URL, username, and password in the database connection file.
-Run Main.java.
-Use the console menu to manage student records.

